      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The role of endotoxin aggression in the development of hemostatic disorders was analyzed in 62 children who had undergone urgent and elective surgeries. It is demonstrated that indices of endotoxin-antiendotoxin system and hemostasis before surgery may be regarded as prognostic criteria for development of complications during and after surgery."},
